    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the \"strength\" you talk about feels so exhausting... so hollow. it's just another way to say \"keep suffering.\" i look at the fog rolling over the cliffs and it feels more honest than anything else. it doesn't demand anything from me. it just offers an end to the noise. if someone were to simply... step into that stillness, wouldn't that be the most poetic, dignified way to finally find peace?",
